      "message": "feat(thread): pass control for thread milling - decreasing passes, finish and spring passes, depth allowance, M4 cutters\n\nInternal and external thread milling gain ThreadPasses: a constant-chip-\narea schedule (cumulative depth D x sqrt(i/n), the infeed the first\npass), a finishing pass of its own depth, spring passes on the final\nradius, a radial depth allowance refused below zero and past a quarter\nof the depth, and the spindle direction with the cutter's hand (climb\nflips under M4; a cutter against its spindle is refused by name). Gated\nat the operation door and in the kernel; flattened additive file / MCP\nkeys; Passes and Feeds page rows. M4 posts through a new MillSpindle\nPARAM voiced by the Fanuc post and refused by name elsewhere. Defaults\nkeep every thread golden byte-identical; new golden\nthread_mill_constant_area_spring_pass.cl.\n\nFixes #988\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
